    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49475": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor of Dental Hygiene",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Clinical Instructor of Dental Hygiene Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Instructor of Dental Hygiene Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit: Cover letter Curriculum vitae or resume Contact information for three professional references Copies of professional licenses and certifications (upon request) The University of South Dakota is committed to creating a welcoming learning and working environment that supports excellence, collaboration, and service to the people of South Dakota. Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution The University of South Dakota Working Title Clinical Instructor of Dental Hygiene Posting Number F01915P Department USD-Dental Hygiene Physical Location of Position (City) Sioux Falls Posting Text The University of South Dakota Department of Dental Hygiene invites applications for a full-time (12-month, 100%) Clinical Faculty position based in Sioux Falls, South Dakota. This position is part of an innovative partnership between the University of South Dakota and Falls Community Health Dental Clinic that combines academic instruction, clinical supervision, and direct patient care in a community health setting. The successful candidate will supervise dental hygiene students during clinical education experiences, and deliver direct patient care during designated clinic sessions. This faculty member will play an integral role in preparing future dental hygienists while advancing access to quality oral healthcare throughout the region. Essential Responsibilities Teaching & Clinical Education Supervise dental hygiene students in the clinical setting while ensuring patient safety and high-quality care. Provide instruction, mentoring, and evaluation of student clinical performance. Facilitate student competency assessments and clinical skill development. Participate in faculty calibration, curriculum development, program assessment, and accreditation activities. Ensure compliance with Commission on Dental Accreditation ( CODA ) standards, South Dakota Board of Dentistry regulations, and University policies. Collaborate with Falls Community Health Dental Clinic staff to coordinate student schedules and clinical learning experiences. Clinical Practice Provide direct preventive dental hygiene services within the scope of South Dakota licensure during designated clinical practice periods. Maintain accurate clinical documentation utilizing the clinic’s electronic health record. Collaborate with dentists, dental hygienists, and other healthcare professionals to provide comprehensive patient care. Support quality improvement, infection prevention, and patient-centered care initiatives. Faculty Service & Professional Engagement Participate in department, university, and community service activities. Maintain professional licensure, certifications, and clinical competency. Engage in professional development appropriate to faculty rank. Demonstrate a commitment to community engagement and service. Displays initiative and willingness to contribute to continuous improvement of clinical education and patient care. Required Qualifications Graduate of a Commission on Dental Accreditation ( CODA ) accredited Dental Hygiene program. Bachelor of Science in Dental Hygiene ( BSDH ). Current South Dakota dental hygiene license or eligibility for South Dakota licensure. South Dakota certification to administer local anesthesia and nitrous oxide/oxygen sedation, or eligibility to obtain certification. Current Healthcare Provider CPR certification. In good standing with the South Dakota Board of Dentistry. Demonstrated commitment to community engagement and service. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, healthcare providers, and community partners. Preferred Qualifications Master of Science in Dental Hygiene ( MSDH ) or a closely related field, or current enrollment in a graduate degree program. Three or more years of clinical dental hygiene experience. Previous preclinical and/or clinical teaching experience in a CODA -accredited dental hygiene program. Experience providing care in public health, federally qualified health center, or other community setting. Knowledge of CODA accreditation standards and outcomes assessment. Work Schedule This is a full-time, 12-month faculty position. Clinical education activities are generally scheduled Tuesday through Thursday during the academic year. The faculty member will also provide direct patient care at Falls Community Health Dental Clinic during designated clinic sessions, anticipated to average approximately one and one-half days per week (Mondays, Fridays). This position offers a unique opportunity to combine teaching, clinical practice, and community service through a partnership between the University of South Dakota and Falls Community Health Dental Clinic. Faculty maintain an active clinical role while educating future dental hygienists, expanding access to care, and strengthening South Dakota’s oral health workforce. The University of South Dakota is committed to fostering an environment of academic excellence, collaboration, innovation, and service. Candidates must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position. Posting Date 08/19/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 09/20/2026 Advertised Salary commensurate with education and experience, plus State of SD benefits package Duration of the Term 12 months If Other, describe duration Appointment Percent 100 Tenure Status Term Proposed Rank Instructor Work Hours Typical Hours Worked Per Week Appointment Type Regular Scope of Search External (includes Internal) If internal, define scope of search Department Description and Cultural Expectations Enrolling over 2,100 students, the USD School of Health Sciences is the only comprehensive School of Health Sciences in the state and is a leader in interprofessional education. The School of Health Sciences is home for eleven graduate degree majors, six undergraduate degree majors, four minors, and five certificate programs. The majors include Addiction Counseling and Prevention, Dental Hygiene, Health Sciences, Medical Laboratory Science, Nursing, Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, Physician Assistant Studies, Public Health, and Social Work. In addition, the SHS is home for two centers: the Center for Prevention of Child Maltreatment and the Interprofessional Health Education Center. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement USD is committed to fostering a dynamic and welcoming working and learning environment for all. USD provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to ideological, political, or sectarian opinions or perspectives; or race, color, creed, religion, sex, ancestry, disability, national origin or any other factor protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws. USD is committed to the principles of free expression and encourages the timely and rational discussion of topics in an environment that is intellectually and ideologically diverse. Contact Information Nicole Solomon Program Assistant I nicole.solomon@usd.edu Working Conditions Cognitive Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the cognitive requirements for this position. Analyzing, Comprehend, Frequent Change, Logic, Memory, Multiple Priorities, Reading, Reasoning, Verbal Communication, Written Communication, Intense Customer Interaction, Multiple Stimuli, Pace-fast, Perform calculations Protective Clothing/Equipment Please check the appropriate response for this position's use of the following protective clothing or equipment. Eye Protection, Latex Gloves, Protective Clothing, Surgical Mask If other protection is used please identify As appropriate for dental hygienist Physical Requirements Please designate the physical requirements of this position Fine Finger Manipulation (keyboarding, pipefitting, bench work, etc), Grasping, Lifting light, Repetitive Motion, Use Both Hands, Wrist Movement (twisting or rotating), Bending, Stooping, Twisting, Driving, Sitting for sustained periods of time, Standing for sustained periods of time, Walking, Climbing Stairs, Reaching, Squatting, Stretching Describe any of the conditions selected Sensory Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the sensory requirements for this position. Hearing, Speaking, Vision (With and without corrective lenses), Depth Perception, Distant Vision, Near Vision, Peripheral Vision Working Conditions & Exposures Working Conditions or Exposures (or potential exposures) that this position may encounter during the course of the work day. Biohazard, Chemical Hazards, Exposure to Infectious Diseases, Radiation, Vibrations, Vaccination recommended due to potential occupational exposure, Walking/Standing on wood, metal or concrete, Exposure or Potential Exposure to Blood/Body Fluids, Exposure to Noise, Work in narrow aisles/passageways Please describe, in more detail, any of the conditions checked above Working Environment Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Classroom Environment, Clinical Environment, Office Environment, Lab Environment If you have indicated Other Environment, if work tasks involve one or more of the above, or if further explanation is necessary, please use the space provided. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Transcripts Other Reference List The South Dakota Board of Regents is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The Board of Regents will take Affirmative Action to ensure that all employment practices are free of discrimination. In addition, the Board of Regents fully supports incorporation of non-discrimination and Affirmative Action rules and regulations into all of its employment practices. Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting the appropriate Human Resources office. Please see the Contact Us section of this webpage for more information. Veterans’ & Disability Preference/Re-employment Rights Campus Security & Crime Statistics Clery Report Position Definitions Notice to all applicants: If you are selected as a finalist, job references and a background check may be conducted. South Dakota Board of Regents 306 E. Capital Ave, Suite 200 Pierre, SD 57501 605-773-3455 Back to top Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49259": {
      "title": "Faculty, QE9811 (Physiology)",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Faculty, QE9811 (Physiology) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty, QE9811 (Physiology) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution The University of South Dakota Working Title Faculty, QE9811 (Physiology) Posting Number F01932P Department Biomedical & Translational Sciences Physical Location of Position (City) Vermillion Posting Text The Division of Biomedical and Translational Sciences at the University of South Dakota Sanford School of Medicine invites applications for an Academic Biomedical Science Educator to teach Human Medical Physiology. This is a 12-month position, tenure track. Degree requirement: Ph.D. in Medical Physiology or closely related field OR Professional Degree at the doctoral level in the healthcare field. Applicants must have experience teaching systems Physiology to health science professionals (MD, PA, PT, OT students). Previous experience with problem-based/active learning pedagogy in a health sciences context is desired. Salary will be commensurate with training and experience. The USD Sanford School of Medicine has announced the move of the first 18 months of the M.D. program and the Division of Biomedical & Translational Sciences from Vermillion to Sioux Falls. Travel between sites may be required until the move is complete. To apply, submit a curriculum vitae, a summary of teaching experience and interests, and contact information for three references. All materials must be posted to the University of South Dakota online employment website at https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu . Review of applications will begin on September 7, 2026, and continue until position is filled. Posting Date 08/04/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 09/07/2026 Advertised Salary Salary will be commensurate with training and experience. 